cff-version: 1.2.0
title: standseg
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper
  describing the algorithm it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Elaine
    family-names: Ye
repository-code: https://github.com/Sugarc0de/standseg
abstract: >-
  A Rust implementation of the multi-resolution forest stand segmentation
  algorithm of Ye et al. (2025), which extends the Harward & Woodcock (1992)
  nested-hierarchical region-growing segmenter to develop micro-segments against
  a second data layer, and of its temporally consistent extension to image time
  series (Ye et al. 2025, IEEE GRSL). Reproduces the original C byte for byte
  on one image, and the reference Python implementations byte for byte on two
  images and on time series.
keywords:
  - image segmentation
  - remote sensing
  - forest stand delineation
  - Landsat
  - region growing
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
